{"schema_version":"1.0.0","metadata":{"trial_id":"202610081400-old-west-saloon-effort-low","prompting_method_id":"concept-build-free.v0","model_id":"claude-sonnet-5-5","seed":11,"server_state_id":"concept-free.v1"},"style":{"name":"Old West frontier saloon","rationale":"Second pass on the Silver Nugget. The design stays the same: gray stone_bricks infill held in a dark spruce timber frame, with warm lantern and banner accents on a dusty red-sand street. The first pass read as a flat box with a plain roof, so the changes are mostly depth and edges. (1) Every face now has a spruce band at the floor line and at the roofline. (2) Full-height spruce log piers are doubled, in the wall plane and 1 block forward, so the facade has vertical rhythm and relief. (3) The sign board is pushed forward and framed by the piers, with wall signs on it. (4) The false front is a stone parapet topped by a stair cornice that overhangs 1 block, which gives a resolved crown. (5) The roof gets eave slabs that overhang the sides, and the rear and side parapets are finished. (6) The entrance bay is left open, with swinging trapdoor doors, lanterns and a lit bar glimpse inside, so the ground floor invites you in. (7) The 3-deep boardwalk porch carries a railed balcony on log posts. It has a front step, hanging lanterns, and props: barrels, a chest, a bench and dead bushes. (8) The street has a hitching rail with a gate, hay, a barrel and a water trough, plus sand patches. Side walls get timber pilasters, windows and floor bands so they are finished too. Openings are aligned to the piers, and the three bays are consistent."},"palette":{"manifest":["minecraft:stone_bricks","minecraft:spruce_planks","minecraft:spruce_log","minecraft:spruce_stairs","minecraft:spruce_slab","minecraft:spruce_fence","minecraft:oak_fence_gate","minecraft:spruce_door","minecraft:spruce_trapdoor","minecraft:lantern","minecraft:glass_pane","minecraft:red_wall_banner","minecraft:blue_wall_banner","minecraft:red_sand","mine